<article class="env-lemma" id="074R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/074R">Lemma <span data-tag="074R">11.6.2</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a finite central simple $k$-algebra. Any automorphism of $A$ is inner. In particular, any automorphism of $\text{Mat}(n \times n, k)$ is inner. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The Skolem-Noether theorem (Theorem <a href="/tag/074Q" data-tag="074Q">11.6.1</a>) applies. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>